# `**/` matters. A bare `node_modules` only matches the one at the context
# root, so every apps/*/node_modules and packages/*/node_modules was being sent
# to the daemon and copied in over the top of the install the image had just
# done. Those are symlinks into .pnpm store paths whose names include a
# per-pnpm-version peer hash, so a host tree built by a different pnpm than the
# image leaves dangling links and the Vite build fails to resolve its imports.
**/node_modules
.git
.github
.husky
.claude
unraid

# Build-context weight. The pnpm store alone is ~300 MB and none of this is
# needed by either image; the capture image mounts screenshots back in at run
# time rather than copying them.
.pnpm-store
.turbo
.idea
screenshots
posters
prerolls
apps/*/dist
# A previous native capture's throwaway database. Copying it in made the
# container start from a tree it then had to delete, as a file it did not own.
**/.harness-data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
